{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1539877-paths-and-personality-traits","id":1539877,"title":"Paths and Personality traits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-05T12:57:02-07:00","id":1539877,"title":"Paths and Personality traits","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I have just finished reading &quot;Tome of the Watchtowers&quot; and &quot;Signs of Sorcery&quot;, and my impression is the in-game consensus is that personality traits determine which path you awaken to, but not all personalities neatly fit onto the 5 path 'stereotypes' for lack of a better word. So some people could awaken to multiple paths (sequentially not simultaneously), and that is why there are Successive awakenings.<br /> <br /> Are there scenarios or statements to the contrary? People not all what the path is about and nonetheless part of it? Could it be the other way around, that anyone can awaken to any path but the path you awaken reinforces certain behaviours and inhibits some others?<br /> <br /> All this rambling came about trying to find our in our group of friends which paths we do belong, and we ended up thinking that some specific set of personality traits would be bad predictors of which paths we would actually want to be; certainly I identify a lot with Mastigos as I understand it, but would enjoy more the Acanthus power set.<br /> <br /> So, how could we answer 'what path am I most likely to awaken?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 08-05-2024, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T13:58:32-07:00","id":1539882,"title":"","content":"Maybe its whatever shakes you out of your status quo. You could have an Obrimos personality, for example, believing that everyone and everything has untapped potential, being someone who is determined to persist or start over as mant times as it takes to achieve your goals. But you keep being sent back to square one by bad luck or poor timing of events, you keep persisting, but eventually it wears at you. So when you find Mystery about breaking through the vagaries of Fate, it draws you so strongly that you Awaken as an Acanthus.<br /> <br /> Your Path reinforces certain behaviors through convenience. An Acanthus doesn't need to spend mana every time to cast improvised spells of Fate and Time, because your Ruling Arcana are reliable tools that you can always fall back upon. So you naturally start thinking in terms of narrative, stories, intent, legalese, tropes, etc. Sure, people might think you have an insane attachment to your lucky gun, but that's because being the only one who fires it is an easy +3 conditional duration to keep its luck enhancements, that lucky habit has a tangible benefit for you.<br /> <br /> The same goes with the Thyrsus having unusual habits, because they might be doing things to garner favor with a certain spirit court, feed their familiar or keep a deal with a certain spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-05-2024, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T14:36:34-07:00","id":1539885,"title":"","content":"I think it's canonically a Mystery, but I've not read the Pentacle book yet. I feel you could definitely express any personality through any arcana though; If you're a more forthright Acanthus you'd take more direct action on fate as opposed to subtle nudges. If you're a studious Mastigos you might mostly cast knowing and unveiling spells despite having very brash options available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28563-hydrophiliak","name":"Hydrophiliak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28563_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T14:56:21-07:00","id":1539890,"title":"","content":"Going by at times by my impulsive personality and going with the flow with most things. I can see myself as a member of the Acanthus path as the most likely scenario.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T18:35:37-07:00","id":1539906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hydrophiliak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1539877-paths-and-personality-traits?p=1539885#post1539885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's canonically a Mystery, but I've not read the Pentacle book yet. I feel you could definitely express any personality through any arcana though; If you're a more forthright Acanthus you'd take more direct action on fate as opposed to subtle nudges. If you're a studious Mastigos you might mostly cast knowing and unveiling spells despite having very brash options available.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, it is something we have seen done and it happens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1539877-paths-and-personality-traits?p=1539890#post1539890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going by at times by my impulsive personality and going with the flow with most things. I can see myself as a member of the Acanthus path as the most likely scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personality wise I would have things from Mastigos mainly, but some Acanthus in there too. I prefer the Fate and Time Arcana when packed together, but my main Arcana would be Mind clearly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T18:40:06-07:00","id":1539907,"title":"","content":"Bolded for emphasis:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1539877-paths-and-personality-traits?p=1539882#post1539882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Maybe its whatever shakes you out of your status quo. </b>You could have an Obrimos personality, for example, believing that everyone and everything has untapped potential, being someone who is determined to persist or start over as mant times as it takes to achieve your goals. But you keep being sent back to square one by bad luck or poor timing of events, you keep persisting, but eventually it wears at you. So when you find Mystery about breaking through the vagaries of Fate, it draws you so strongly that you Awaken as an Acanthus.<br /> <br /> <b>Your Path reinforces certain behaviors through convenience.</b> An Acanthus doesn't need to spend mana every time to cast improvised spells of Fate and Time, because your Ruling Arcana are reliable tools that you can always fall back upon. So you naturally start thinking in terms of narrative, stories, intent, legalese, tropes, etc. Sure, people might think you have an insane attachment to your lucky gun, but that's because being the only one who fires it is an easy +3 conditional duration to keep its luck enhancements, that lucky habit has a tangible benefit for you.<br /> <br /> The same goes with the Thyrsus having unusual habits, because they might be doing things to garner favor with a certain spirit court, feed their familiar or keep a deal with a certain spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>These were our main idea and conclusion respectively. Even if you are personality wise very dour and serious, once you get Life and Spirit as ruling Arcana, you start looking at the world in terms of what is easy for you to cast. Same goes with every other path and arcana.<br /> <br /> So we wondered is the Personality that shapes the Path, or is the Path that shapes the Personality? I found a reference in the Boston book of a mage that had a strange awakening, and it seems to be the Path shaping the Personality, every other example I can think of, seems that the Personality was set, then came the Path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T11:40:38-07:00","id":1539935,"title":"","content":"The Paths do have a lot of flavour, maybe that bleeds through more when you have lower wisdom? They'd colour your perceptions and mage sight anyway so they'd definitely have an impact on your personhood. Knowing you can just heal yourself may mean you're more likely to take risks to physical injury etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28563-hydrophiliak","name":"Hydrophiliak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28563_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T15:45:36-07:00","id":1539953,"title":"","content":"I prefer the Fate, Mind, Space and Time Arcana myself as they speak to me the most. The magic is subtle for the most part and I can see some elements of the Thyrsus path that could fit way better then the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T18:21:26-07:00","id":1540025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1539877-paths-and-personality-traits?p=1539953#post1539953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer the Fate, Mind, Space and Time Arcana myself as they speak to me the most. The magic is subtle for the most part and I can see some elements of the Thyrsus path that could fit way better then the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same with the four Arcana, but in my case I see some Obrimos too.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T21:41:44-07:00","id":1540032,"title":"","content":"Funny how we can see ourselves in multiple genres or magic types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}